    "history_and_evolution": "The word \u2018Ceramic\u2019 came from the Greek term \u2018Keramos\u2019, meaning pottery. Ancient Egyptians discovered tiles could be hardened and waterproofed via kiln firing. Mesopotamians added artistic value with terra-cotta and ceramic wall decorations.",
